&lt;p&gt;When registering EC2 instances as capacity for an ECS cluster, you can use Bottlerocket as the operating system for these instances.
If you want to understand the AWS console workflow, start with the &lt;a href="https://piyush-jena.github.io/previews/bottlerocket/current/en/os/1.51.x/install/quickstart/aws/ecs/#aws-console-quickstart"&gt;video &lt;em&gt;Amazon ECS: Using Bottlerocket&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/a&gt;
Otherwise, read the &lt;a href="https://piyush-jena.github.io/previews/bottlerocket/current/en/os/1.51.x/install/quickstart/aws/ecs/#aws-cli-quickstart"&gt;AWS CLI Quickstart&lt;/a&gt; or the pattern &lt;a href="https://containersonaws.com/pattern/ecs-ec2-bottlerocket-cluster"&gt;Amazon ECS cluster on Bottlerocket&lt;/a&gt; which outlines how to start Bottlerocket with &lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/"&gt;SAM CLI&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Amazon EKS</title><link>https://piyush-jena.github.io/previews/bottlerocket/current/en/os/1.51.x/install/quickstart/aws/k8s/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://piyush-jena.github.io/previews/bottlerocket/current/en/os/1.51.x/install/quickstart/aws/k8s/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;




